"converter_title" = "BorgVR Dataset Import";

/* Subtitle of dataset import view */
"converter_subtitle" = "Importing Volume Data";

/* Instructions shown on the converter view */
"converter_instructions" = "To begin the data import process, tap **Select Input Volume** and choose the volume to import:\n\n- **QVIS Volume**: Select a `.DAT` (metadata) file and its corresponding `.RAW` (volume data) file. This format **requires conversion**.\n- **NRRD Volume**: Select a `.NRRD` or a `.NHDR` (metadata) file and its corresponding volume data file. This format **requires conversion**.\n- **BorgVR Native Volume**: Select the `.DATA` volume file. This format is **copied without conversion**.\n\nDue to restrictions in the **iOS App Sandbox security system**, you need to **manually select all files involved**. If you are importing a QVIS or NHDR volume you need to select both the **metadata file** and the **volume data file**. When copying a native BorgVR, just select the `.DATA` file.\n\nIf you are importing a volume, enter a **description** for the dataset before proceeding. Then, tap **Start Conversion** to convert the data into a **bricked hierarchical format**, optimized for BorgVR rendering. If you are importing a BorgVR native volume, simply tap **Copy Data** to store the files in the app’s private space for high-performance visualization.";

